{number: 138}
{title: Where Jesus Is,’Tis Heaven}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Since [Ab] Christ my soul from sin set free,
This world has [Db] been a heaven to [Ab] me;
And 'mid earth's sorrows and its woe,
'Tis [Eb7] heaven my Savior here to [Ab] know.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [Db] hallelujah, yes, 'tis [Ab] heaven,
'Tis heaven to know my sins for-[Eb7] given;
On [Ab] land or sea, what-[Db] e'er be-[Ab] fall,
Where Jesus [Eb7] is, 'tis heaven for [Ab] all.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Once [Ab] earth seemed dark and full of gloom,
Now [Db] flowers of joy and peace a-[Ab] bloom;
The clouds are gone, the sky is clear,
Since [Eb7] Jesus came and brought me [Ab] cheer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
'Tis [Ab] heaven to walk with Him each day,
'Tis [Db] heaven to hear Him softly [Ab] say,
"Fear not, My child, I'm by thy side,"
In [Eb7] Him my soul is satis-[Ab] fied.
{end_of_verse}
